  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale  \n   The goal is to minimize the maximum overlap of a step function, constrained by integral 1. The current construction on 280 points achieves C5\u22480.381375. This solution is obtained by locally optimizing a random-guess initial shift of the parent solution. Local optima likely prevent improvement. To escape them, we use a mathematically grounded non-local search called generating set descent, which explores symmetric shifts of the solution. By systematically varying the function shape and leveraging symmetries, we can find lower global minima.  \n\n2. Mathematical Specification  \n   - Variables: h \u2208 \u211d\u207f, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2211h[i] = N/2 (N = 2n_nodes)  \n   - Objective: C5 = max\u2096 \u2016h \u2297 (1 \u2212 h)\u2016\u2081 (discrete mode='full') scaled by dx  \n   - Constraints: Normalization (integral=1) and bounds [0,1]. Feasibility ensured by projection.  \n\n3. Implementation Procedure  \n   a. Input: seed (42), budget_s (100s), **kwargs (parent solution if available).  \n   b. Initialization: Start with provided parent if exists; otherwise use uniform random initialization.  \n   c. Search: Use `scipy.optimize.minimize(method='SLSQP')` for local descent.  \n   d. Global exploration by cycling through generating sets of shifts:  \n   - Shifts: \u00b11, \u00b11/dx, \u00b1(dx\u00b3/\u03c0)  \n   - Each generating set shift is used to explore a local neighborhood.  \n   e. Feasibility: Post-optimization clip values to [0,1] and scale to meet integral  \n   f. Post-processing: Validate solution and re-evaluate C5.  \n\n4. Search Choices and Variations  \n   - Base resolution: n_points = 280 (provided parent)  \n   - Generating set shifts: [-1.0, 1.0, -1.0/dx, 1.0/dx, -1.0/dx\u00b2, 1.0/dx\u00b2, -1.0/dx\u00b3, 1.0/dx\u00b3]  \n   - Other shifts: Scale shifts by \u00b1\u03c0.  \n\n5. Budget and Robustness  \n   - Time allocation: 90s for generating set descent, 10s for initial validation.  \n   - Falls back to parent solution if optimization fails.  \n   - Metrics: Track best C5 during iterations, stop when time exhausted.  \n\n6. Validation and Return Contract  \n   - Validate solution: Check \u222bh = 1 and \u22650.  \n   - Output: (h_values, C5_bound, n_points)  \n   - Final re-evaluation of the best candidate.",
